\newlabel{app:tests}{{D}{16}{Every Registered and Declared Test}{appendix.D}{}}
\newlabel{tab:app-codes}{{12}{16}{From internal code and tier to the name and label used in the main text. A1 and PH6 were supported on held-out papers only weakly and are demoted to exploratory in the main text: A1 does not survive Holm across the six secondary held-out tests (0.063), and the PH6 wave test leans on the six keywords inspected first}{table.caption.62}{}}
\newlabel{tab:app-tests}{{13}{19}{Every registered and declared test. Estimates in pp within topic and year (H1d: change in the new-architecture share for prior-year FM adoption from 0 to 100\%; keyword and wave rows: against all other papers of the same year). Discovery intervals $\pm $1.96 SE; the held-out H1d interval uses $t(G-1)$ quantiles. $p_1$: held-out one-sided $p$; Holm-adjusted, it is unchanged except for H2b$'$ and H2c$'$ (0.0010 each) and E1 (0.0050). MDE80: held-out minimum detectable effect at 80\% power, registered unless marked, with power at the discovery effect for E1 and P1b in parentheses; $^f$ discovery MDE80 from the frozen dry run; $^d$ derived post hoc ($2.49\times $SE), with no reading rule; n.c.\ not computed. $^u$ unregistered held-out row (Table~\ref {tab:app-unreg}). $^n$ null-frame $p_1$ 0.020; two-sided $p$~0.063. $^i$ intersection-union $p$ for $0<b<1$. $^t$ not a test (PH7: title style had been explored before registration). $^a$ computed analytically in the declared run ($2.49\times $SE). Tiers as at the start of this appendix; main-text labels in Table~\ref {tab:app-codes}; reading rules in the text}{table.caption.65}{}}
\newlabel{tab:app-main}{{14}{20}{The herding account tested at three points, in full: each observable, its internal code and the sign predicted by imitation and by continuity (in parentheses: its mechanism or reference point, or a named alternative: lock-in, priority; $\cdot $: none). Percentage points unless the row states otherwise (row 1: counts; row 3: twins per paper per 1,000 submissions; row 6: percentile points; row 11: slope $b$), 95\% intervals, within topic and year (keyword rows and row 11: against the same year's other papers). Held-out tests are one-sided and confirm direction, not size, so a supported test can have an interval that includes 0. Codes: P only earlier data; same-year: twins are concurrent papers, so not only earlier data; \Hok /\Hno {} registered hindsight variants pass/fail; R retrospective by construction; \Tok {} held after link removal. Tiers as at the start of this appendix; rev.: reversed registered prediction; prim./sec.: declared primary/secondary held-out test (six secondary tests in all, among them rows 11, 12 (Emerging), 16 and 17, one-sided and unadjusted; under Holm across the six they give 0.019, 0.063, 0.026 and 0.052); D/C: discovery-only gap whose registered held-out test was not supported. The continuity predictions were written after the tests had run. Main-text labels in Table~\ref {tab:app-codes}}{table.caption.66}{}}
\newlabel{tab:app-ph6}{{15}{21}{PH6: weighted mean over waves of a keyword's acceptance gap after minus up to its share peak, pp; 2,000 within-year permutations. Held-out papers before and after peaks: 454 and 1,022}{table.caption.72}{}}
\newlabel{tab:app-unreg}{{16}{22}{Unregistered held-out rows: reported, not interpreted. Two-sided, unadjusted $p$; $^i$ intersection-union $p$; $^o$ one-sided. Estimates in pp unless noted. P5 and P6 change sign or size between splits and are not interpreted; they are listed so that the count of 17 rows is complete}{table.caption.74}{}}
\newlabel{tab:app-pooled}{{17}{22}{Pooled re-run (exploratory; confirms nothing). pp unless noted. Pooled Holm or $q$ values: H1d $3\times 10^{-4}$; H3a 0.098; FL level $q$ 0.14 (trend $p$~0.18); E2 0.036; P2 0.063. The discovery outputs remain the registered record}{table.caption.76}{}}
